# Implementation Plan - Dynamic Subject/Chapter/Topic in Materials Service

This plan outlines the steps to replace hardcoded subject and material data in [materials-service.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/views/materials-service.tsx) with dynamic data fetched from the database, mirroring the logic used in the `question-bank` view.

## Proposed Changes

### [api]

#### [MODIFY] [services.ts](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/packages/api/src/routers/home/services.ts)
- Add `getMaterials` procedure to `serviceRouter`.
- This procedure will fetch subjects, chapters, and topics, similar to `getMcqQuestionBank`.

### [home]

#### [MODIFY] [materials-service.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/views/materials-service.tsx)
- Update tRPC call to use `trpc.home.service.getMaterials.useQuery()`.
- (Previous changes still apply: replace hardcoded data, handle loading/empty states, etc.)

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1. Navigate to the Materials Service page in the browser.
2. Verify that the "Concept Book" and "Marked Book" sections now display subjects and chapters (as materials) fetched from the database.
3. Verify that the counts (e.g., "10 টি", "15 পৃষ্ঠা" - though pages will be placeholder for now) are consistent.
4. Verify that the loading state is shown while data is being fetched.
5. Verify that the "View All" button and other interactive elements still function as expected.
